The Go rendering: a command that encodes values each with a field nothing writes,
through json.Marshal, through a function of the program that hands its parameter to
json.Marshal, through a dependency module's function named Marshal, through
xml.Marshal and through encoding/json/v2, some fields tagged to leave a zero value
out, among them fields of types with methods. It hands other values to three
dependency functions whose names say nothing of encoding but that call
json.Marshal: a wrapper named Render, a request context's JSON method, and Emit,
which encodes what a method of the command returns through the dependency's
interface. It prints another value through fmt. A test encodes a value of its own,
and encodes and fills a value of the command. The dependency is a local module the
target requires and replaces, so the rendering loads with no network access.

